#  Windows Fundamentals – Part 1

This document introduces the basic concepts of Microsoft Windows operating systems, focusing on system structure, navigation, users, permissions, and essential tools for cybersecurity and penetration testing.

---

##  What is Windows?

Microsoft Windows is a graphical operating system developed by Microsoft. It is widely used in:
- Personal computers
- Enterprise environments
- Corporate networks
- End-user systems

Windows provides both a GUI (Graphical User Interface) and CLI (Command Line Interface) for system management.

---

##  Why Windows Matters in Cybersecurity?

- Most enterprise systems run Windows
- Active Directory environments are Windows-based
- Many attacks target Windows services
- Understanding Windows helps in privilege escalation and lateral movement

---

##  Windows File System Structure

Windows uses a hierarchical structure organized into drives.

### Common Directories:


C:
├── Windows # System files
├── Program Files # Installed applications (64-bit)
├── Program Files (x86) # 32-bit applications
├── Users # User profiles
└── Temp # Temporary files


